# Version control and local configuration
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*

# Python environments, caches, builds, and test output
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.eggs
build
dist
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage*
htmlcov

# Development-only files and runtime output
# tests/ and scripts/ ARE needed in the build context: they are inputs to the
# QUALITY_RECEIPT.json tree digest, which the "quality-receipt" Dockerfile stage
# recomputes. That stage is the only place they land; neither reaches the runtime
# image, which copies just the verified receipt out of it.
#
# NEVER exclude a digest input. The full set is src/, tests/, scripts/,
# pyproject.toml, uv.lock, mypy.ini and ruff.toml (see scripts/quality_receipt.py).
# Excluding one here does not fail loudly: the gate stage recomputes a digest over
# fewer files and reports "the tree does not match its receipt", which reads like a
# stale receipt and is not one.
*.log
logs
*.pid
.cache
tmp

# The pixi environment is ~2 GB of toolchain that the `mojo-kernels-enabled` stage installs for
# itself; shipping it through the build context would be slower than rebuilding it.
.pixi
**/__mojocache__
src/plantgeo_ml_service/method/kernels/_native
